! Test v0.92.0: water wB97X-D / STO-3G + C-PCM(water) geometry
! optimization -- the range-separated + PCM combination enabled in
! v0.92.0 (phase 3c).
!
! Reference (1 thread, reference netlib BLAS/LAPACK; STO-3G keeps
! the per-primitive HRR under the default %hrr_mode auto):
!   Final energy: -75.321150034933 Ha   (5 optimization steps)
! The 'Final energy' line and the breakdown 'Total energy' line must
! AGREE (the dispersion double-count fixed in v0.89.0), and the CHG
! dispersion at the optimum is about -2.89e-5 Ha.
!
! Validation behind this test (BENCHMARK_NOTES_v0.92.0.md): the
! analytical RS+PCM gradient reproduces the central-FD PCM gradient
! to 1.5e-5 (RKS, C-PCM and IEFPCM) and to the pre-existing ~1e-4
! open-shell class (UKS, same as B3LYP+PCM); the wB97X+C-PCM
! solvation shift of this molecule (-3.33 kcal/mol) sits next to the
! B3LYP one (-3.28).
%method  WB97X-D
%basis   sto-3g
%job     opt
%pcm     cpcm
%solvent water
%charge  0
%mult    1
%geom angstrom
O 0 0 0.1173
H 0 0.7572 -0.4692
H 0 -0.7572 -0.4692
*end
